# `engine/build.rs` applies these to the bindgen submodule by matching each
# hunk's context against the source exactly, so a checkout must not rewrite
# their line endings. `core.autocrlf` is on by default in Git for Windows and
# would otherwise do just that.
#
# This is belt and braces: `build.rs` normalises to LF as it reads, because the
# submodule's sources go through the same matching and no `.gitattributes` here
# can reach inside a submodule.
engine/third_party/patches/*.patch -text
